course: dictionary
lesson: 9454
title: Many meanings of star
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word star has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. «Stars have different colours: the hottest are blue-white, our Sun is yellow-white.» Here a star is a huge ball of burning gas that makes its own light.
explain: «The Sun is one of billions of stars in our galaxy, the Milky Way.» Look at the words around star: they tell you it is a giant ball of gas in space, not a shape or a sticker.
explain: «She is a star in the new film.» Here a star is a very famous actor. Check by swapping in your meaning: "She is a famous actor in the new film" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Star can also be a verb. To star in a film is to have a main part in it, so stars, starred and starring all come from the same word.
fact: A star is a huge ball of burning gas far away in space. We see it as a bright point in the night sky.
fact: The Sun is a star, and it is the closest star to Earth.
fact: Stars give their own light. Planets do not give their own light; they shine because sunlight falls on them.
fact: A group of stars is called a constellation.
fact: Star can also mean a shape with five or more points, a gold sticker for good work, or a very famous actor, singer or player.
exercise: Which of these is a star? | Mars | *The Sun | The Earth | The Moon
exercise: Mia draws a shape with five points for her sticker chart. What shape is it? | A square | A circle | *A star | A triangle
exercise: «Her film made her a star.» What does star mean here? | *A very famous actor or singer | A bright light in the night sky | A gold sticker for good work | A shape with four corners
test: «Stars have different colours: the hottest are blue-white, our Sun is yellow-white.» What colour is our Sun? | Blue-white | Red | *Yellow-white | Orange
test: Which thing makes its own light? | *A star | A moon | A planet | A rock
exam: In «The Sun is one of billions of stars in our galaxy, the Milky Way», what is the Sun? | A moon | A galaxy | *A star | A planet
